{
 "schema": "runecraft.rune_mechanics",
 "version": 1,
 "date": "2026-10-30",
 "status": "design proposal; numbers are prototype assumptions, not balance",
 "sources": {
  "v4": "design/source_package/RuneCraft_Rune_Ability_Function_Plan_MVP_v4.md",
  "user": "user decisions 2026-10-30 (override v4): one distinct unlock per grade; Fire G1 hit / G2 burn / G3 trail; volcano = summon spouting lava blobs, Electric makes blobs hop; combine 2 runes = grade up; runes cost mana, towers cost mana stone; graft removal returns contents, fee burns; extra status interactions allowed; no craft preview; abilities per rune = natural count (min 2 besides hit), unlock spread over grades, unlock fast; balance to be set; Mana rune: grafting it earns mana (damage -> mana, later a mark that turns all damage around the marked enemy into mana); mana stones are collected as enemies die",
  "proposal": "Claude's choices where the user left room: unlock grades, extra abilities marked proposal, numbers, interactions marked proposal"
 },
 "principles": [
  "Each rune has its natural abilities only (hit + at least 2 more, more where the theme gives more, e.g. Ice). Abilities unlock between G1 and G5, mostly by G2-G4; grades without a new ability are stat growth. Each ability is one graft slot.",
  "Every ability produces an event; a graft subscribes to that event and applies the donor's open abilities there.",
  "A donor contributes only abilities open at its own grade. Its vehicle (projectile / summon) never travels; only effects do.",
  "Grafts on load/stack abilities fire when the load's effect happens (tick, threshold, discharge), never when a stack is merely added.",
  "Chain/hop takes the shape of the host carrier: projectile bounces, lava blob hops, flame leaps, fragment re-aims.",
  "Siblings are order-independent: payloads merge first, then propagators carry the merged payload; sibling propagators never trigger each other.",
  "No pair-specific code. A 13th rune is a JSON entry.",
  "Propagation power (chain/area/fragment falloff) scales Damage and ForceMove distance; statuses are carried unchanged."
 ],
